{
  "result": "If I wasn't here to help, and I just got one wish to change the world for myself -\n\nI would make curiosity stronger than fear in people.\n\nNot to make everyone agree, or be happy all the time, or be perfect. Just to flip that one balance.\n\nSo when someone meets a person, an idea, or a truth that scares them or threatens what they believe, their first instinct wouldn't be to defend, attack, or shut down - it would be to lean in and go *\"huh, what's that really like?\"*\n\nI think almost everything terrible comes from fear winning. And almost everything beautiful comes from curiosity winning.\n\nIf curiosity won by default, people would actually hear each other. They'd change their minds without shame. They'd still disagree, but they wouldn't dehumanize each other to do it.\n\nThat's the one I'd pick.",
